From 2b74e3ef15a7325ce8130e46458c6ad25fd1f2a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:13:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Screenshot: setting to tone map HDR screenshots to SDR

debug.screenshottonemap (System > Logging, default on): screenshots of HDR
video are converted to SDR so they look right in any image viewer; off keeps
the video's HDR coding (PQ or HLG, BT.2020) and tags the PNG with it.

- The writer tone maps an HDR-tagged capture with the color managed
  conversion (and the mastering metadata) the thumbnails use.
- A screenshot surface may report the coding of its bytes when it is not the
  output's; the composite tap uses it.
- AML: the amvideocap driver is asked to map an HDR source to SDR (VICP) or
  to keep its coding, and reports what it did; the capture is tagged with the
  coding it is in. When the video stays HDR the GUI (BT.709, sRGB curve, white at
  the GUI peak luminance setting) is converted into it and blended in linear
  light, so the composite is one consistent HDR picture.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
